WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is
an Emmy-Award winning acto

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.437
you know from his iconic rol
as The Fonz on "Happy Days,"

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as shows like "Arreste
Development" and "Barry."

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.942 line:92%
He stars in "Monsters at Work,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
with new episodes streamin
Wednesdays on Disney+.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.514 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, I know bowlers!

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't call me
"No Splits Fritz" for nothing.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They -- They call you that?
-For nothing.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Huh! I never heard them
call you that.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they do,
they do, they do.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:26.192
And we've got Pin Pal Val
over there and No Gutter Cutter.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.763
Hmm. Duncan doesn't play,
but he loves the snachos!

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
our very good friend
Henry Winkler.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hello, Henry!

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-Good. You can --

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You're not here.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can take your mask off
Henry.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right, right. Okay.
You know what?

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:46.279
There's a mandate now -- we have
to wear it inside in L.A.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no!

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.716
See, this is what happens when
not everyone gets vaccinated

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to wear it
in your own home.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.821
-Yeah. You know what?
It is shocking, but here we are.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:59.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I was alive
when polio struck America,

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't hear
one person say,

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, I don't think
I'm gonna take the vaccine."

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.167 size:88% position:44%
-That was a different --
It was a different time.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.835 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It was a simpler time.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.170 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yes. And no more polio.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There we go.
You haven't heard

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
hide nor hair of polio
for a great time.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?
I'm very happy to see this

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you have actually
given them to me,

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I know exactly
what I'm looking at.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.549 size:84% position:42%
You are an accomplished
children's book author,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have some
right behind you.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
-And this is no joke.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've written -- Is it
over 30 books at this point?

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:34.027 size:78% position:39%
-Yes, yes, 37 novels
with my partner, Lin.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, for -- Starting
in the second grade --

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:42.602
Well, first grade, second grade,
and all the way to sixth grade

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And look what else
I have sitting on my books

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.041 line:92%
Because -- Congratulations

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.276 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have
just made Amber's day,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
not that anybody needs
to make her day.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's the happiest person
I know.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She is --
and uses the word "what"

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
better than anybody
I've ever met.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
She should teach just "what" -

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.692 line:92%
a "what" class at Juilliard.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:08.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll tell ya --
And it's difficult

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.796 line:92%
because, you know, I try -

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
When she's not around,
I try very hard

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.069 line:92%
to steal the use of "what,

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I should just
leave it alone.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it is lovely,
I will say --

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:25.845
It's lovely to hear your voice
in an animated show like this.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.546 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I'm wondering --

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:29.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you have five
grandchildren, and obviously -

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One on the way.
-One on the way, as well!

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, I'm assuming
they're not too engaged

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.690 line:92%
with your work like "Barry,"

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
but do they enjoy
the new monster show?

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what? They do,
but I did force them.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-I do --

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:50.436 line:92%
No, I have soldered the remote

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.672 line:92%
to Disney+ just for that.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:57.777 size:81% position:41%
But it is so much fun
because people love --

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all ages --
love "Monsters, Inc."

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.916 line:92%
And the "Monsters at Work"

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
takes place right after
the movie's finish.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.822 line:92%
And Billy Crystal is in it

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.059 size:81% position:41%
John Goodman is in it.
Ben Feldman is in it.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mindy is in it.
It's just great.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.463 line:92%
-Now, what about "Happy Days"?

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a show
I grew up with as a kid.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has that sort of
permeated its way

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:26.039 size:81% position:41%
into your grandkids'
viewing habits at all?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Two years ago,
my oldest grandson, Ace,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
I showed up at his house
because I --

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like to be there
when they're trick-or-treating

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sit on their doorstep
and hand out candy

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
to all the children
that come with them.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:45.124 line:92%
And he was dressed as The Fonz

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.393 line:92%
He had on the pleather --

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whatever it's called.
The fake leather.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.864 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He had on the jeans.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.767 line:92%
His red hair was slicked back.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.004 line:92%
My heart fell out of my body

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.707 line:92%
-Did you say his name was Ace?

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:03.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that's the rare case
of someone with a name

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.912 line:92%
that's cooler than The Fonz.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He is.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:11.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just won his championship
baseball game.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:11.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Great.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:16.623 size:88% position:44%
-First pitch, first hit
of the season, home run.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:21.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they went on
to win the championship.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.861 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, my God.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I made them
those books, you know --

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.499 size:78% position:39% line:92%
snap fly, a chat fly.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.934 line:92%
You know what I'm talking about?

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:32.572
-I love when I'm so confiden
it's not a paid endorsement.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:37.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, it isn't,
because I -- I had to pay.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got, you know --
But I made them those books.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.183 line:92%
And Jules, his younger brother

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:47.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
also had his first
baseball season.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.757
-That's fantastic. I'm gla
that things are going so wel

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the entire Winkler clan.
I have more questions.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.861 line:92%
We're going to be right back

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
with more from our friend
Henry Winkler.

